## Recharts Visualization Standards

### Chart Styling Configuration
```typescript
// Axis ticks: 12px Inter, rgba(238,242,247,.72)
// Grid: rgba(127,140,162,.22)
// Lines: strokeWidth=2, dot=false
// Areas: gradient to rgba(255,198,46,.18)
// Bars: radius [6,6,0,0], barCategoryGap 28%, maxBarSize 28
// Tooltip: compact, tabular-nums, show Δ vs prev period
// Legend: pill badges, keyboard focusable, aria-pressed
```

### Mock Data Requirements
- Series: up to 90 data points, 2-3 series per chart
- Tables: 80-120 rows, client-side pagination (10/20/50)
- Filters: all state local-only (no network calls)
- Performance: memoize selectors, pre-aggregate per filter dimension

## Accessibility Standards (WCAG 2.1 AA)

### Implementation Requirements
- Semantic HTML elements with proper roles
- Visible focus rings (accent color outlines)
- aria-labels/roles for interactive elements
- Screen reader summaries for charts ("role=img" with description)
- View-as-table toggle for chart data accessibility
- Modal focus trap with Esc to close
- Full keyboard navigation support
- Color contrast ratios meet AA standards

### Testing Requirements
- Playwright E2E for modal accessibility and keyboard flows
- Vitest unit tests for component behavior
- No CLS on modal open/close transitions
- Focus returns to originating element on modal close

### Acceptance Criteria
- Skills collapsed by default, expand animates correctly
- Six dashboards open fullscreen via shared-element
- Layout/spacing pixel-consistent across breakpoints
- Keyboard + screen reader flows fully supported

## Security Headers & CSP

### Required Security Configuration
```typescript
// next.config.js security headers
const securityHeaders = [
  {
    key: 'Content-Security-Policy',
    value: `
      default-src 'self';
      script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-inline';
      style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
      img-src 'self' data: https:;
      font-src 'self';
    `.replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim()
  },
  {
    key: 'X-Content-Type-Options',
    value: 'nosniff'
  },
  {
    key: 'Referrer-Policy', 
    value: 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin'
  }
];
```

## CI/CD Pipeline Requirements

### GitHub Actions Workflow
1. ESLint → TypeScript check → Vitest units → Next.js build
2. Lighthouse CI with budget gates
3. Playwright E2E tests
4. Preview deployment to Vercel
5. Performance monitoring and alerts

### Quality Gates
- No TypeScript errors
- All tests pass
- Lighthouse scores meet targets
- Bundle size within budget
- No accessibility violations

